algorithm_fidelity.derives_eom_from_vari.reason:
The core.py docstring states the Yee-type discrete action, and the Numba kernels implement exactly its Euler-Lagrange equations in the paper's explicit form:
- discrete Klein-Gordon with Wilson lines (Eq. 16/B3);
- Maxwell-Ampère (B11) and the discrete Lorenz condition (B10);
- Gauss-law initialisation for A1;
- Noether charge and current (Eqs. 18 and 20);
- energy (Eqs. A18-A20).
Methodology 2.1 explains the variations. The extensions are also variational: the Pauli term adds Δt²μσ·B̄ψ to the KG bracket plus magnetisation currents. I checked that the coded current μ(M_{z,i+1}-M_{z,i-1})/2Δx equals δS_P/δA2. No non-variational PDE discretisation is used.

algorithm_fidelity.yee_type_field_layout.reason:
The field layout matches the paper's Sec. II Yee lattice, restricted to 1D with a single transverse cell as in the original's 1D runs:
- φ on vertices i;
- A0 on time-like edges at half-integer times (A0m/A0p);
- A1 on x-edges i+1/2;
- A2 and A3 on the transverse edges attached to vertex i;
- Ex on time-like faces (i+1/2, n+1/2);
- Bz and By on spatial faces, computed as link differences.

