boundary_boundary_test_1.first_principle.reason:
The argument holds at each step:
- without a magnetic moment the zero-point cyclotron energy is not cancelled by -μ_B B;
- relativistically this enters as E0² = m²+|qB|;
- the line is red-shifted by qB/2m² for B≪Bc (I verified the expansion, and SymPy check 2d confirms it) and by 20.0% at B=Bc;
- the error is independent of discretisation because the field content of the action is unchanged.
The threshold ħω_c/mc² ≳ 2ε_tol follows correctly.

