boundary_boundary_test_2.first_principle.reason:
The reasoning is correct at each step:
- φ=0 is an exact fixed point of the linear KG equation at fixed A;
- a Bogoliubov map of a classical state with occupation n gives 2n|β|², while the quantum vacuum gives (2n+1)|β|²;
- the classical scheme therefore captures exactly the stimulated part.
I checked the algebra (|α|²=1+|β|²), and SymPy checks 3a/3b confirm it.

